    "timing": "20 Hz quantization of intended 0, 1/30, .1, .2, .3 seconds. It is not bit-exact float scheduling of the original frame engine. Damage stops at tick 6; persistent final entity expires at tick 60.",
    "damage": "Preserves source 500:100:35:15 ratios around the existing Minecraft base direct damage 20. Actual infected loss also uses existing CombatScale; heavy vehicle armor applies its existing multiplier. Original transformation/weapon multipliers and friendly-fire factors are not ported.",
    "contact": "Record UUID before hurt, across all rings, persistent through NBT reload. Existing enemy/owner/crew/PvP checks, hull armor, event cancellation and loaded-world ray obstruction remain authoritative.",
    "save": "Version 1, age 0..60, strict UUID list with 4096-record save guard. This guard is not claimed to match original CollisionActionBehaviour capacity. Elapsed unloaded world time skips old stages instead of replaying damage; rollback/stale/malformed state expires.",
    "presentation": "One initial production explosion receipt and impact cue. Interpolated radial streaks follow radius knots 1/4/7/9; smoke fades for 60 ticks. Source effect identities are not decoded; existing procedural flashes, debris and smoke remain authored Minecraft visuals.",
    "aiClearance": "Expands the existing aircraft explosive safety candidate region to MAX_RADIUS+2 = 11, accounting for the new outer ring.",
    "worldDamage": "Existing permission-controlled block blast runs once at existing radius 4. Original WorldDamage and ThreatBall records remain evidence, not new permission or block-destruction authority."
  },
  "remaining": [
    "Original impulse units (9000/-10000, 6000/-7500, 3500/-5000 and random terms) are recorded but not guessed into Minecraft knockback.",
    "Original effect identities, sound-bank patch resolution, .433333-second AIMessage/camera shake, and full threat/world damage behavior remain open.",
    "Hover/weapon selection, independent rapid unguided rack, original player capacities, full helicopter motion/actions and dedicated multiplayer remain open."
  ]
